          "id": "923.c.multiply",
          "part": "c",
          "operation": "multiplication",
          "set": "Q",
          "closed": true,
          "answer": "Closed.",
          "proof": "For x=a/b and y=c/d with b,d != 0, xy = ac/(bd). Integer products supply the numerator and denominator, and bd != 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "923.c.divide",
          "part": "c",
          "operation": "division",
          "set": "Q",
          "closed": true,
          "answer": "Closed on the explicitly permitted nonzero divisors.",
          "nonzero_divisor_required": true,
          "proof": "Let x=a/b and y=c/d, with a,b,c,d in Z and b,d != 0. The source requires y != 0, hence c != 0. Then x/y = ad/(bc), a ratio of integers whose denominator bc is nonzero. This includes x=0 and negative operands.",
          "domain_note": "No claim is made that division is defined on Q x Q without the stated restriction."
        }
      ]
